      "writtenOn": "2021-03-18T15:12:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ard: it\u0027s a list of algorithms that Samsung was/is using, so they would want the GKI to have them all. Pixel only needs these three: sha256, hmac(sha512) and cbc(aes). I believe it boils down to what the certification agency advises for the particular OEM. The Samsung list would make the majority of OEMs happy, I was told.\n\nEric: I can put the list in the code, but there\u0027s no strict criteria apart from Gossamer saying \"all SHA and all HMAC, AES ECB/CBC/GCM, and a DRBG\".",
      "parentUuid": "c4552386_983f5b9b",
      "revId": "79b5e3de99d315b7be8ab2206915f31a405c4d2c",
